Z||000000||Wolfhound||03-20-2001||06:29 AM||||I was driving to Atlanta yesterday in my pickup and was caught in traffic in the right hand lane. I suddenly heard a high pitched whine and my truck did a little wobble as this car came by. He was going easily over a hundred and I couldn't believe what I saw.<BR>It was a white GT racer with quickchange rearend, which is all I saw with the exception of Evans on the left rear.<BR> Looked on the net this morning and found it! <A HREF="http://www.evansautomobiles.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.evansautomobiles.com</A> <BR>Dang it! I don,t have a 150,000 dollars.<BR>I think the actual car I saw is in their galary, 4th photo down on the right.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||03-20-2001||09:23 AM||||Schweeet!!!<BR>I've seen a lot of "stuff" around Atlanta, but I've never seen one of those cars. <BR>I was surprised when I found their address. Most of the high performance builders and tuners and hot rodders seem to be in the Northern or waaayyy Southern 'burbs. These folks appear to be very close to Atlanta. What part of town were you in? <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
